/*
:name: spec_memory_poweron_not_reset
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: spec_memory_poweron_not_reset
:pyrope_top: spec_memory_poweron_not_reset
:v2prp_native_expect: refuted
*/
// SPEC (docs 08-memories.md): "A `reg` array's initializer means exactly what a
// scalar `reg`'s does: it is the **reset value** of every entry, and it is the
// power-on contents too (the `initial` contents -- the wrapper's `INIT` parameter /
// a Verilog `initial` block)." and "`initial=` alone, which is then power-on
// contents only."
// Rule encoded here: the emitted Verilog of `reg mem:[4]U8 = 3` carries the reset
// (driven by the module's single Reset `zap`) AND an `initial` block; the `initial`
// block is power-on contents only, so re-reading that Verilog must not turn it
// into a second reset. The golden declares no power-on contents (an unknown start
// is a don't-care on the reference side), so the pair must PROVE.
// The prp-v2prp2v native leg runs the other direction (this Pyrope as the
// reference, the golden's round trip as the implementation): there the
// reference's power-on contents face an implementation that has none, which is
// REFUTED-cex (:v2prp_native_expect: refuted).
pub mod spec_memory_poweron_not_reset(ck:Clock, zap:Reset, we:Bool, a:U2, d:U8, ra:U2) -> (q:U8@[0]) {
  reg mem:[4]U8 = 3
  q = mem[ra]
  if we {
    mem[a] = d
  }
}
